# engine-strict is deliberately NOT set.
#
# With it on, npm turns every EBADENGINE *warning* into a fatal error — for the
# whole dependency tree, transitive dev tooling included. That broke the Coolify
# deploy on 2026-09-15: nixpacks then built on Node 22.19.0, `lint-staged` raised its
# floor to >=22.22.1, and `npm install` aborted. lint-staged only ever runs in a
# git pre-commit hook on a developer's machine — it is never executed in the
# container — so gating the production build on its Node floor bought nothing and
# cost a deploy.
#
# Without it, npm warns and carries on, which is the right severity for "a package
# in the tree prefers a newer Node than this machine has".
#
# The deploy now runs NIXPACKS_NODE_VERSION=24 (decision 01M59PK8QMF1B7Z8BMMDMD6PH5),
# a major-only pin whose patch moves with nixpacks. Bringing the strict check back
# is the owner's call: first confirm the deployed `node -v` from the deploy log
# clears every engines floor (see AGENTS.md, Quality gates, for the one-liner).
